# Architecture (MVVM)

## Layering

- Put code in its package under `com.noshitechinc.restaurant`: `feature/<name>/`, `domain/{model,repository,usecase}/`, `data/{remote/api,remote/dto,mapper,repository}/`, `core/{common,ui,network,auth,logging,designsystem,adaptive}/`, `navigation/`, `di/`.
- Keep the dependency direction `feature` → `domain` ← `data`; `core/*` is usable by all layers.
- Keep `domain` pure Kotlin: no Android, Compose, Retrofit or DTO imports.
- Never import `feature`, `data` or `domain` from `core/designsystem`; error-aware UI (`ErrorState`, `LoadStateContent`, `AppScaffold`) belongs in `core/ui`.
- Declare repository interfaces in `domain/repository`, implement them as `…RepositoryImpl` in `data/repository`, bind with `@Binds` in `di/`.
- Repositories return `ApiResult<DomainModel>`; only repositories call Retrofit services.
- Add a use case in `domain/usecase` only for cross-repository or business logic; otherwise the ViewModel calls the repository directly.

## ViewModel

- Declare `@HiltViewModel class XxxViewModel @Inject constructor(...) : BaseViewModel()`.
- Expose `val uiState: StateFlow<XxxUiState>` backed by a private `MutableStateFlow`; `XxxUiState` is an immutable data class updated with `copy`.
- Give each independently loaded section its own `LoadState<T>` (`Idle`, `Loading`, `Content(data)`, `Empty`, `Error(error: AppError)`); convert results with `ApiResult.toLoadState()`.
- Hold user-facing text as `UiText` (`Resource(@StringRes id, args)` or `Dynamic(value)` for sanitized server text).
- Never put `Context`, `Resources` or Compose types in a ViewModel; never use `runBlocking`.
- Send one-off events with `sendEffect(...)` into `effects: Flow<UiEffect>`. Base effects are `ShowMessage(text, tone)` and `ShowErrorDialog(error)`; `UiEffect` is an open interface, so declare feature effects as `data class`/`data object` implementing it.
- Run every mutation through `launchSubmit(key) { }`: re-entry with the same key is ignored, the key is always released, unexpected exceptions become `AppError.Unknown`.
- Drive button loading from `submittingKeys: StateFlow<Set<String>>` collected in the Route: `val submitting by viewModel.submittingKeys.collectAsStateWithLifecycle()`, then pass `"save" in submitting` to the button's `loading`. `isSubmitting(key)` is a non-reactive snapshot; use it only in ViewModel logic and tests. Never keep a separate `isSaving` flag.
- Report mutation failures with `presentError(error)`: `NoInternet`/`Timeout` become a transient `ShowMessage`, everything else a `ShowErrorDialog`. Session end is not handled here: `TokenAuthenticator` calls `SessionManager.endSession()`, whose `sessionEnded` is observed in `AppNavHost`. Load failures go into the section's `LoadState.Error`.

## Route and Screen

- Split every screen in `feature/<name>/XxxScreen.kt` into `XxxRoute` and `XxxScreen`.
- `XxxRoute(viewModel: XxxViewModel = hiltViewModel(), onNavigate…)` collects `uiState` with `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` and wraps the screen in `AppScaffold(effects = viewModel.effects, onEffect = { … }, requiresNetwork = …)`.
- `XxxScreen(state, onAction…, modifier)` is stateless: no ViewModel, no `hiltViewModel()`, no flows. It owns all previews.
- Trigger navigation through Route callbacks; emit a navigation effect only when navigation depends on a result.
- Declare destinations as `@Serializable` types in `navigation/Destinations.kt` and register them in `AppNavHost`.
- Use the `scaffold-screen` skill to create a new screen.
